# Frontend Architecture Contract

This rule is mandatory for every Cursor task on this project. Audit-only and planning-only tasks must not modify application code. Implement only the approved phase, then stop and wait for review.

## 1. Mandatory pre-implementation inspection

Before coding:

1. Read this architecture rule.
2. Inspect the target route, page, feature, existing shared components, relevant shadcn primitives under `src/components/ui/`, providers, locales, and configuration.
3. Search for existing functionality before creating files or components.
4. Present blockers and scope conflicts before proceeding.

Do not invent requirements, API contracts, permissions, or business rules to unblock yourself. Stop and ask.

## 2. Approved architecture

```text
src/
├── app/                    # App bootstrap, router, providers
├── layouts/admin/          # Admin shell, sidebar, header, navigation
├── pages/
│   ├── auth/
│   └── admin/              # Route-level page composition only
├── features/<feature>/     # Feature UI, hooks, API, query keys, schemas, types, logic
├── components/
│   ├── ui/                 # shadcn/ui primitives only
│   ├── shared/             # App-level compositions from shadcn (e.g. FilterBar, PageHeader)
│   ├── data-table/         # Genuinely reusable table infrastructure
│   ├── filters/            # Specialized shared filters; do NOT duplicate shared/FilterBar
│   ├── charts/             # Shared charts only when used by multiple features
│   └── forms/              # Reusable form infrastructure only when justified by real reuse
├── lib/                    # Shared infrastructure (incl. HTTP client when approved)
├── store/                  # Client/UI state only (Redux)
├── mocks/                  # Explicitly identified mock data and handlers
├── types/, constants/, config/  # Global definitions only
├── locales/en/, locales/ar/     # All user-facing strings
└── index.css               # Global CSS and design tokens (unless migration approved)
```

Rules:

- Do not create files just because a directory exists.
- Do not introduce additional layers or alternate folder conventions without explicit approval.
- Keep feature-specific components inside `features/<feature>/` by default.
- Promote to `components/shared/` (or specialized shared folders) only with genuine cross-feature reuse.

Note: Vite entry may import `src/App.tsx` today. New bootstrap work belongs under `src/app/`. Do not relocate `App.tsx` unless the task explicitly authorizes it.

## 3. File creation and modification control

For each task:

- Define exact scope before implementation.
- List proposed files to create and modify.
- Create only files required by the approved task.
- Do not move, rename, delete, or duplicate files without explicit authorization.
- Do not add speculative abstractions or placeholder files.
- Do not change unrelated modules.
- Stop if the work requires an unapproved architectural change.

## 4. shadcn/ui policy

- Reuse `src/components/ui/` and `src/components/shared/` before creating anything new.
- Do not reimplement an existing shadcn primitive as a custom component.
- Keep `src/components/ui/` limited to shadcn primitives and explicitly approved customizations.
- Application compositions belong in `shared/` or the owning feature — never inflate `ui/`.
- Native semantic HTML is acceptable when appropriate (e.g. landmarks, sr-only labels, overlay dismiss controls).
- Do not import `radix-ui` / Radix primitives outside `src/components/ui/`.
- Prefer `@/` path aliases. App code prefers `cn` from `@/lib/utils` (UI CLI files may import `"cn"`).
- Do not regenerate, overwrite, or bulk-modify shadcn components without explicit scope approval.

## 5. Dependency boundaries

| From | May import | Must not import |
|------|------------|-----------------|
| `pages/` | Owning feature, shared/specialized components, `lib`, layouts (sparingly) | Other pages' internals |
| `features/A` | `ui`, `shared`, specialized components, `lib`, `store`, own modules | `features/B`, unrelated features |
| `components/ui/` | `lib` utilities, external UI deps | pages, features, layouts, shared |
| `components/shared/` (and data-table/filters/charts/forms) | `ui`, `lib`, locales/i18n | features, pages |
| `store/` | Pure client state | Axios/Query/API side effects in reducers |

- Avoid circular dependencies.
- Do not create duplicate HTTP clients, query clients, providers, or global utilities.

## 6. State and data ownership

- TanStack Query owns remote/server state.
- Redux owns client/UI state only.
- Axios is the standard HTTP client.
- React Hook Form + Zod are preferred for forms where appropriate.
- Do not invent API endpoints, payloads, response schemas, permissions, or business rules.
- Use a real API only when its contract exists or is explicitly approved.
- Mock data and mock auth must be clearly labeled; never present mocks as production security.
- Never persist passwords or embed real secrets in frontend code.
- Do not place API calls inside Redux reducers.
- Keep query keys and API logic in the owning feature unless genuinely global.

## 7. Localization and accessibility

- Every new user-facing string must go through i18n (`src/locales/en` and `src/locales/ar`).
- Preserve RTL/LTR support.
- Prefer existing Label, Input, Button, Dialog, Select, and other suitable shadcn primitives.
- Maintain semantic HTML, keyboard access, visible focus, and accessible form errors.

## 8. Routing, providers, and global configuration

Do not modify routing, providers, layouts, global CSS/design tokens, TypeScript aliases, Vite config, or dependencies during an unrelated feature task.

Such changes require: (1) documented reason, (2) exact affected files, (3) impact analysis, (4) explicit approval or authorized task scope.

## 9. Mandatory completion report

After each implementation phase, report:

- Files created / modified / renamed / deleted (renames/deletes only if authorized)
- Existing components reused
- Any deviation from the approved plan
- Lint, type-check, and build results (name commands not run)
- Static checks vs browser/runtime checks
- Known limitations and remaining work

Never claim browser verification unless it was actually performed.

## 10. Stop conditions

- Audit tasks remain audit-only; planning tasks remain planning-only.
- Implement only the approved phase; do not auto-continue to the next phase.
- If requirements conflict, stop and ask for clarification.
- After the requested phase and verification, wait for review.
